      "verdict": "“A psyker from a sealed Chapter with locked archives. Courteous, never flaunts his rank, though he has an unpleasant habit of holding that heavy stare a beat too long in conversation. I have loathed sorcery since the Siege, but the field arithmetic is simple. While cover rises out of the ground, a force dome hangs overhead and torn flesh knits on the move, his place in the line is justified. That held until the end of the Vertis operation, an episode I scrubbed from my onboard logs. When Brother Limsiar of the Flesh Tearers broke into the genetic madness of our blood, I walked him through the scope. I watched Chaplain Raphael try to pin him down out of sight, only to be disarmed and put on his back. I watched the thing that had been Limsiar burst toward the rise by the fortress, where the Watch Reclusiarch, Black Templar Stalver Forge and Librarian Callidus blocked his path. My finger lay on the trigger, waiting for Raphael's order. It never came to a shot. The three of them dragged him down and the Reclusiarch carried out the sentence on the spot. But for that one second, three heads shared my reticle. The Reclusiarch knew our flaw by virtue of his office. The Templar and the Librarian were surplus witnesses to the shame of Sanguinius's sons. Since that day Callidus's grey head has never strayed far from my crosshairs. If he lets so much as half a word slip, I will be the one to squeeze.”"
